    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.09_minimal_category_theory.chapters.07_mittens_as_colimit_anchor.sections.01_eleven_leg_diagram.concrete_anchor_9_Mammal#mammal" .
silm:instances_papers_09_minimal_category_theory_chapters_07_mittens_as_colimit_anchor_sections_01_eleven_leg_diagram_concrete_anchor_9_Mammal#mammal silm:hasLongDescription "The Mammal is the supraclass node Mammal in the lineage chain DomesticCat -> Mammal -> Animal. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Mammal', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
